WEBVTT

00:00:01.054 --> 00:00:12.932
Yes, I embraced tenderness and devotion
sou itooshisa to kizuna wo daita

00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:18.639
Floating in unending space
hatenaki umi ni ukabu

00:00:18.639 --> 00:00:25.568
On this small planet
chiisa na hoshi de

00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:37.115
When I feel your warmth next to me
anata no nukumori wo soba ni kanjiru toki

00:00:37.291 --> 00:00:43.230
I understand the burden
inochi no omosa to

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:50.636
And the transience of life
hakanasa wo shiru no

00:00:53.407 --> 00:00:58.445
Nights of sorrowful wandering
mayoinageku yoru mo

00:00:58.445 --> 00:01:05.319
And tearful mornings
namida no asa mo

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:10.924
I believe in tomorrow
ashita wo shinjiru kara

00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:17.197
So I can make it through
koeteyukeru no

00:01:17.197 --> 00:01:25.627
To the continuation of the dream
yume no tsuzuki he

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:38.585
A stone called the "Fragment"

00:01:38.585 --> 00:01:41.488
discovered in Clairmont
more than 100 years ago...

00:01:41.488 --> 00:01:44.582
A mysterious research
organization called the Ged Group.

00:01:45.659 --> 00:01:47.227
Detective Cooks,

00:01:47.227 --> 00:01:50.897
the head office sent you to
investigate the disappearance of

00:01:50.897 --> 00:01:52.888
several children from Nohedge.

00:01:53.066 --> 00:01:55.728
Why are we going to Clairmont?

00:01:56.069 --> 00:01:58.401
What's the connection?

00:01:58.572 --> 00:02:01.166
You remember that old recording?

00:02:01.341 --> 00:02:03.543
The one in my room.

00:02:03.543 --> 00:02:05.306
Yes?

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.083
That recording has been copied onto this.

00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:12.052
The sound is bad.

00:02:12.052 --> 00:02:15.613
But after all, it was recorded
more than 100 years ago.

00:02:16.556 --> 00:02:20.660
It shows the transformation
of Professor Radcliffe,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.152
a talented young physicist
with a promising future.

00:02:24.297 --> 00:02:27.596
He was also a friend of my
grandfather who was a reporter.

00:02:30.203 --> 00:02:34.264
The year 1901, the 12th of May.

00:02:34.574 --> 00:02:37.134
The sound is terrible.

00:02:41.581 --> 00:02:46.575
THE CHILDREN OF BEFORT

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.857
The year 1901, the 12th of May.

00:02:50.857 --> 00:02:54.127
My friend, Bob Cooks, a reporter
with a Westland newspaper,

00:02:54.127 --> 00:02:56.288
came to visit me early this morning.

00:02:57.097 --> 00:02:58.962
Radcliffe!

00:02:59.566 --> 00:03:02.729
1901 CLAIRMONT

00:03:02.803 --> 00:03:05.872
Hello, Cooks! Don't have
any scoops for you.

00:03:05.872 --> 00:03:08.875
The frontier of science
is in Europe right now.

00:03:08.875 --> 00:03:12.003
Radcliffe, I have something
I want you to look at.

00:03:12.846 --> 00:03:14.848
Cooks was strangely agitated

00:03:14.848 --> 00:03:17.282
as he told me about a mysterious incident.

00:03:17.717 --> 00:03:19.912
A stone? It's completely black.

00:03:19.986 --> 00:03:23.089
A few days ago,
five white-haired children...

00:03:23.089 --> 00:03:25.080
passed away.

00:03:26.092 --> 00:03:29.755
And I was there when it
happened, completely by chance.

00:03:32.599 --> 00:03:35.268
I happened to see some strange children

00:03:35.268 --> 00:03:37.759
at an abandoned factory outside of town.

00:03:59.659 --> 00:04:03.330
The children made such a bizarre sight,

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.958
I aimed my camera at them
without thinking about it.

00:04:17.043 --> 00:04:20.046
W-Who are you children?

00:04:20.046 --> 00:04:22.139
What in the world are you doing here?

00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:54.037
When I came to, all five of
them were lying there naked.

00:04:54.481 --> 00:04:56.915
This stone was on the ground nearby.

00:04:57.083 --> 00:04:59.252
There were several smaller pieces as well,

00:04:59.252 --> 00:05:02.522
but while I was bringing them
here they suddenly disappeared.

00:05:02.522 --> 00:05:04.046
Disappeared?

00:05:04.824 --> 00:05:08.954
At the insistent request of my friend,
I started experimenting on the stone.

00:05:20.874 --> 00:05:25.004
There were no signs of injury or
poison found on the children.

00:05:25.078 --> 00:05:28.048
The cause of death was never
discovered, it was listed as unknown.

00:05:28.048 --> 00:05:31.211
The bodies were identified
and sent back to their families.

00:05:35.188 --> 00:05:37.424
And their hair wasn't white,

00:05:37.424 --> 00:05:40.825
it was apparently just ordinary
blonde or brown hair.

00:05:41.094 --> 00:05:43.296
One surprising thing was that

00:05:43.296 --> 00:05:45.526
all five of them were from Europe.

00:05:45.565 --> 00:05:50.059
Why would those children come
to this far off southeastern island?

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.607
It's not surprising that my
friend should find it suspicious.

00:05:53.607 --> 00:05:58.840
He felt there had to be some secret,
obscure reason for what happened.

00:05:58.878 --> 00:06:03.178
He wasn't satisfied with how easily the
whole incident was explained away.

00:06:05.752 --> 00:06:07.354
Using x-ray technology

00:06:07.354 --> 00:06:09.956
is very popular in the scientific
community at the moment.

00:06:09.956 --> 00:06:12.481
And I am also fascinated
with experimenting with it.

00:06:12.859 --> 00:06:15.862
Conrad Rugen's discovery
of this new form of radiation

00:06:15.862 --> 00:06:18.431
is causing a tremendous change
in the dark world that has existed

00:06:18.431 --> 00:06:20.365
ever since the middle ages.

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.869
The power of science

00:06:22.869 --> 00:06:26.703
will put the darkness of confusion and
chaos under the shining light of day.

00:06:27.273 --> 00:06:31.539
Stripping away the fears
and blind faith of mankind.

00:06:32.746 --> 00:06:36.682
Science will replace god and
become the new religion.

00:06:37.417 --> 00:06:40.215
There is nothing that cannot be
understood through science.

00:06:44.791 --> 00:06:47.661
Even the reason for the sudden
death of those five children,

00:06:47.661 --> 00:06:51.062
will someday be easily explained.

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:56.603
The 15th of May.

00:06:56.603 --> 00:06:58.972
In order to investigate the
composition of this substance,

00:06:58.972 --> 00:07:00.974
I am going to irradiate it with x-rays.

00:07:00.974 --> 00:07:02.942
I don't expect there to be
anything unusual about it,

00:07:02.942 --> 00:07:06.002
I think it's just a piece of
some kind of mineral.

00:07:06.613 --> 00:07:08.672
Three minutes exposure.

00:07:32.739 --> 00:07:35.071
What is this?

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:41.581
For a whole week, all the while
increasing the x-ray exposure time,

00:07:41.581 --> 00:07:43.883
I transferred the strange pattern
that rose up from inside this stone

00:07:43.883 --> 00:07:46.477
onto photographic plates.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:49.787
Seventy-eight plates in total.

00:07:51.291 --> 00:07:53.293
What does this mean?

00:07:53.293 --> 00:07:55.761
Is this the discovery of a new mineral?

00:07:56.029 --> 00:07:59.265
I was completely puzzled by
the constantly changing pattern

00:07:59.265 --> 00:08:03.998
found in a piece of stone only
twenty centimeters long.

00:08:04.671 --> 00:08:08.801
I suggested that a full-scale investigation
should be started immediately.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.646
The year 1902, the 8th of March.

00:08:13.646 --> 00:08:15.949
The royal science ministry has
named this black piece of stone

00:08:15.949 --> 00:08:17.851
the "Fragment."

00:08:17.851 --> 00:08:19.953
In order to examine it more thoroughly,

00:08:19.953 --> 00:08:22.285
a special research organization
has been established.

00:08:22.689 --> 00:08:25.425
The name of the organization is
being taken from the demon god Ged

00:08:25.425 --> 00:08:29.462
in our country's ancient myths.
It's being called the Ged Group.

00:08:29.462 --> 00:08:33.133
The country's surprisingly enthusiastic
support of the project is because

00:08:33.133 --> 00:08:35.435
they see it as a chance to
increase our country's power.

00:08:35.435 --> 00:08:39.038
They think this is some kind
of deliberately encrypted code

00:08:39.038 --> 00:08:41.472
from an enemy nation.

00:08:42.642 --> 00:08:45.445
Well, this is the Ged symbol but...

00:08:45.445 --> 00:08:48.414
Detective, do you really believe
that this old organization

00:08:48.414 --> 00:08:50.405
is still in operation?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:54.211
I'd also like to meet
Gherta, that lady director.

00:08:54.254 --> 00:08:56.890
Do you suspect the Phantom Ged
Research Center on Ketplaque Island

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.359
- of something?
- The year 1915.

00:08:59.359 --> 00:09:01.361
The year 1915?

00:09:01.361 --> 00:09:03.196
Time is flying by.

00:09:03.196 --> 00:09:06.324
That's right around the
time of the first World War.

00:09:08.201 --> 00:09:13.640
In order to get more precise records,
we are periodically taking the Fragment,

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:18.168
affixing x-ray devices on all sides of
it, and irradiating it inside a lead box.

00:09:18.411 --> 00:09:20.113
November.

00:09:20.113 --> 00:09:24.317
Tens of thousands of pages of code
have been extracted from the Fragment.

00:09:24.317 --> 00:09:26.486
However,

00:09:26.486 --> 00:09:29.322
not even one could be deciphered.

00:09:29.322 --> 00:09:31.654
It's all complete chaos.

00:09:31.758 --> 00:09:34.249
It's all total nonsense.

00:09:34.427 --> 00:09:37.030
I'm even starting to question
if it can be called a code.

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:40.932
A code found today becomes
something else tomorrow.

00:09:41.134 --> 00:09:44.535
They look like some kind of cells.

00:09:45.405 --> 00:09:47.373
Damn!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.908
Professor Radcliffe, you
dropped something.

00:10:02.188 --> 00:10:05.258
For some reason, my
eyes were drawn to it.

00:10:05.258 --> 00:10:08.094
A local English newspaper dated 1856

00:10:08.094 --> 00:10:11.664
that I found in the old
newspaper section of the library.

00:10:11.664 --> 00:10:17.159
The deaths of the missing
white-haired children.

00:10:17.503 --> 00:10:20.940
I remembered what Bob Cooks had said.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:23.343
That when the children, whose
hair had been white, passed away,

00:10:23.343 --> 00:10:26.938
their hair color had already
changed back to blonde and brown.

00:10:27.046 --> 00:10:29.182
It seemed that the federal
police and the science ministry

00:10:29.182 --> 00:10:31.017
had already done a good deal
of investigating into the children

00:10:31.017 --> 00:10:34.077
because of the mystery of
the symbols in the Fragment.

00:10:34.187 --> 00:10:36.356
However, the cause of their deaths,

00:10:36.356 --> 00:10:40.349
the mystery of why and how they
made their voyage from Europe,

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:44.619
and what the connection was between
the children, was never understood.

00:10:44.831 --> 00:10:48.101
The only things known for certain were
that these children had gone missing

00:10:48.101 --> 00:10:50.370
at the age of five, seven
years before they died,

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:56.104
and then one day they gathered
together in that place and died.

00:10:56.476 --> 00:11:00.546
Even the statements of their families
indicated that while they were alive,

00:11:00.546 --> 00:11:03.344
their hair color was
closest to white in color.

00:11:06.853 --> 00:11:09.055
The year 1918.

00:11:09.055 --> 00:11:11.491
Having come to a dead end
in deciphering the code,

00:11:11.491 --> 00:11:16.053
I spent three years walking through
Europe after the World War,

00:11:16.396 --> 00:11:19.729
in pursuit of the white-haired children.

00:11:21.668 --> 00:11:25.365
The year 1856 in Luanne, France.

00:11:29.208 --> 00:11:33.179
The year 1806 in Newbury, England.

00:11:33.179 --> 00:11:36.783
The year 1771 and 1753 in Cartagena,

00:11:36.783 --> 00:11:40.019
and then Toledo, Spain.

00:11:40.019 --> 00:11:43.756
Italy, the year 1701, Ravenna.

00:11:43.756 --> 00:11:49.395
The years 1682, 1661
and 1642, in Germany.

00:11:49.395 --> 00:11:54.059
Holland, the years 1627 and 1611.

00:12:05.511 --> 00:12:09.615
The evidence of the existence of
these strange white-haired children

00:12:09.615 --> 00:12:12.982
increases in frequency the
farther back in time I go.

00:12:16.155 --> 00:12:19.092
All five of them live for 11 years.

00:12:19.092 --> 00:12:21.959
At the age of 11 they die.

00:12:22.295 --> 00:12:27.995
Even here in Romania, there
are records of them in 1581.

00:12:38.211 --> 00:12:42.113
Andrew Chaseman's portrait!

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:48.309
I found a portrait of a white-haired boy.

00:12:54.727 --> 00:12:58.865
He looked exactly like the child in
the picture Bob Cooks had taken!

00:12:58.865 --> 00:13:01.732
It was the same boy!

00:13:18.051 --> 00:13:19.882
Befort.

00:13:21.421 --> 00:13:24.356
The name of an old village in Belgium.

00:13:27.527 --> 00:13:30.630
In the corner of a bookshelf in a
decaying church, I found the journal

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:32.765
of a university instructor.

00:13:32.765 --> 00:13:38.304
The year 1489, the 12th of September.

00:13:38.304 --> 00:13:42.741
"Seven white-haired
children taken by the devil."

00:13:43.176 --> 00:13:46.839
I couldn't find records
going back any further.

00:13:47.947 --> 00:13:52.475
Befort. The Children of Befort.

00:13:57.156 --> 00:13:59.192
The Children of Befort...

00:13:59.192 --> 00:14:02.462
-Professor! Professor Radcliffe?!
-What's the matter?!

00:14:02.462 --> 00:14:04.530
Just look! From these records alone,

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.499
you can see that they've
appeared 13 times in 500 years!

00:14:06.499 --> 00:14:09.900
Dying... Reawakening...
Children who live on and on!

00:14:10.002 --> 00:14:12.038
The Children of Befort

00:14:12.038 --> 00:14:16.338
appear again and again and
interfere with peoples' lives.

00:14:16.375 --> 00:14:19.278
The code in that fragment.

00:14:19.278 --> 00:14:23.049
A book of revelations?
Or the words of the devil?

00:14:23.049 --> 00:14:27.353
They aren't dead. After a few
decades they arise from their graves,

00:14:27.353 --> 00:14:30.189
sneak into homes with
children, murder the children,

00:14:30.189 --> 00:14:32.316
and become part of the family.

00:14:32.992 --> 00:14:34.857
He's insane!

00:14:34.894 --> 00:14:36.429
Yes, I guess so.

00:14:36.429 --> 00:14:40.166
The year 1919, the 15th of February.

00:14:40.166 --> 00:14:42.896
"The Madness of a Deranged Scientist."

00:14:43.236 --> 00:14:48.608
He dug up the graves of five children
who had been buried 18 years earlier

00:14:48.608 --> 00:14:52.169
and burned the skeletal remains.

00:14:52.712 --> 00:14:56.115
Radcliffe was kicked out of the Ged
Group as a result of his insane behavior.

00:14:56.115 --> 00:14:58.117
Amidst nightmares of monsters,

00:14:58.117 --> 00:15:00.253
he continued his research
in a state of paranoia

00:15:00.253 --> 00:15:03.017
and passed away at the
age of seventy eight.

00:15:03.122 --> 00:15:04.757
And so ended the life of

00:15:04.757 --> 00:15:08.060
a man who believed in science and
whose talent held such promise.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:11.230
How much of this do you
actually believe?

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:16.602
But there really are five white-haired
children who are missing.

00:15:16.602 --> 00:15:20.006
When I saw this picture
of Flo at the head office,

00:15:20.006 --> 00:15:22.341
it reminded me of what
happened with my grandfather,

00:15:22.341 --> 00:15:25.211
and I immediately asked to
be assigned to the case.

00:15:25.211 --> 00:15:26.979
There must be something out there.

00:15:26.979 --> 00:15:29.782
That's why I'm going to
Clairmont to investigate it again,

00:15:29.782 --> 00:15:33.775
the mystery of the code in the
Fragment and the Children of Befort.

00:15:34.086 --> 00:15:38.250
CLAIRMONT SANATORIUM

00:15:41.928 --> 00:15:44.730
In a place so faraway
it seems like a dream,

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:47.166
a resting place is waiting for me.

00:15:47.166 --> 00:15:49.157
I know it.

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:53.603
My spirit will once again have a home,

00:15:53.839 --> 00:15:58.299
a place where sleep and night
and stars are waiting for me.

00:16:00.479 --> 00:16:02.208
Big Brother!

00:16:06.152 --> 00:16:08.721
Let's play hide and seek!

00:16:08.721 --> 00:16:11.524
Soreto's not here yet, right?
Where's Hasmodye?

00:16:11.524 --> 00:16:13.856
He should already be here.

00:16:27.873 --> 00:16:31.309
-I'm going in.
-Will you be okay on your own?

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:46.754
Oh, my! Who are you?

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:50.624
Are you Andrew's friend?

00:16:52.298 --> 00:16:55.401
I've been looking for
Andrew for a while now.

00:16:55.401 --> 00:16:57.892
Where could he be hiding?

00:16:59.372 --> 00:17:01.863
Mistress, have you found him?

00:17:02.241 --> 00:17:04.176
-Who are you?!
-Goodness!

00:17:04.176 --> 00:17:06.412
-Hey! Don't you go running in...
-Hasmodye!

00:17:06.412 --> 00:17:08.175
Hasmodye!

00:17:17.056 --> 00:17:18.785
Hasmodye!

00:17:31.971 --> 00:17:34.906
Hasmodye! Hasmodye!
Are you all right?!

00:17:46.052 --> 00:17:47.519
Hasmodye!

00:17:51.457 --> 00:17:54.427
It's no good! It won't come off!
Hasmodye!

00:17:54.427 --> 00:17:58.796
Mother! This is where
Big Brother was hiding!

00:17:59.298 --> 00:18:02.825
Oh, Andrew! So this is where you've been.

00:18:03.002 --> 00:18:05.664
I've been looking for you for a while now.

00:18:05.871 --> 00:18:09.642
Andrew, you shouldn't
make your mother worry.

00:18:09.642 --> 00:18:14.477
Come, little master, your
tea is ready for you.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:23.010
What's the matter, Andrew?
Are you not feeling well?

00:18:23.189 --> 00:18:25.714
You look like you might have a fever.

00:18:32.932 --> 00:18:34.456
Mother...

00:18:40.706 --> 00:18:42.367
Hasmodye!

00:18:42.608 --> 00:18:45.644
-Aghi...
-Where's the record!?

00:18:45.644 --> 00:18:48.704
Hasmodye, where's your memory record!?

00:19:08.401 --> 00:19:11.029
Hasmodye! Quickly!

00:19:16.075 --> 00:19:18.737
Do it quickly!

00:19:25.551 --> 00:19:28.042
These people...

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:33.115
These people...

00:19:34.093 --> 00:19:37.187
They loved me.

00:19:38.931 --> 00:19:43.368
And I loved them, too.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.669
This hand, this smell,

00:19:48.073 --> 00:19:51.099
this person's heartbeat.

00:19:51.944 --> 00:19:54.847
Everyone was so kind.

00:19:54.847 --> 00:19:57.577
-I...
-Andrew.

00:19:58.451 --> 00:20:00.749
Big Brother.

00:20:02.555 --> 00:20:04.523
Andrew.

00:20:06.792 --> 00:20:09.226
Little master.

00:20:10.863 --> 00:20:12.763
Aghi...

00:20:13.332 --> 00:20:17.428
Is it wrong for me to be here?

00:20:18.003 --> 00:20:20.437
To stay here?

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:22.735
Aghi!

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:17.529
My home.

00:21:34.346 --> 00:21:36.109
Have you recovered?

00:21:39.718 --> 00:21:42.312
Are you all right, Hasmodye?

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:47.760
Hasmodye! We all understand, don't we?

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.923
Who we are, and what it is we're doing?!

00:21:51.063 --> 00:21:53.799
Getting caught up in things
like that is just foolish!

00:21:53.799 --> 00:21:55.501
Hesma!

00:21:55.501 --> 00:21:59.335
Don't let them get to you.
You have to remember yourself.

00:22:02.074 --> 00:22:05.711
I... wouldn't have cared.

00:22:05.711 --> 00:22:09.181
Stop it, Hasmodye!
Do you want to end up like Palza?!

00:22:09.181 --> 00:22:11.342
I don't want to hear things like that!

00:22:35.341 --> 00:22:45.148
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea
fukaku fukaku sukitooru umi no soko ni

00:22:45.417 --> 00:22:55.060
A small flower is resting
chiisana hana madoronderu

00:22:55.060 --> 00:22:59.793
The melody of a gentle wind
amayaka na kaze no shirabe

00:23:00.032 --> 00:23:04.867
Passes through a rainbow
niji wo kuguri

00:23:05.137 --> 00:23:14.273
The fish are playing in the sky
sakanatachi wa sora ni asobu

00:23:14.513 --> 00:23:19.585
Everyone plays the music of love
dare mo ga ai wo kanaderu

00:23:19.585 --> 00:23:24.657
A warm light came down
atatakana hikari futteta

00:23:24.657 --> 00:23:29.060
(A gaze) That gaze
(manazashi wa) sono manazashi wa

00:23:29.294 --> 00:23:33.599
Is unbound and becomes full
hodokete michiteku

00:23:33.599 --> 00:23:38.468
Embraced by water
mizu ni dakare
